      <title>I'm donated my stem cells in Manchester and gave someone years more to live</title>
      <link>https://www.manchesterworld.uk/news/people/im-from-manchester-and-gave-someone-years-more-to-live-through-this-important-donation-5448418</link>
      <description>Fred Baxendall, 33, from Didsbury, made a life-changing difference for a total stranger through stem cell donation, after signing up to the stem cell donor register with blood cancer charity DKMS. Fred has now teamed up with DKMS to encourage others to do the same, and to bust myths about who is or isn’t eligible to register.</description>
